talk - line conference

usage: talk [-n] [room]

    Without a number it lists rooms then asks for one.
    At the room prompt "<room> TALK>", empty Enter redraws the list.
    . aborts / leaves.
    -n  visits rooms with unread and shows them in a row.
    talk N enters a room. The log is kept. This is separate from chat.

    In a room, each line is written to the log and streamed to occupants
    (when you have a seat).

    The three venues (chat / talk / notes/mail/news) share the same keys.
    In speaking venues (chat / talk) you prefix with "/".
      /i  show the list (rooms)  * empty Enter also redraws
      /q  leave (. / q also work)
      /?  help (/help also works)

    /who     seats and knocks
    /title   title (leader)
    /open /close /lock  open/close (leader)
    /knock   ask for a seat
    /seat id grant a seat (leader)
    /kick id remove (leader)
    /ra      show all lines (asks to confirm when many)

    In-room keys are Wick-specific (the "/" command style). We will align
    once the original talk -? is available.
